+# Checklist: create-and-scene
+
+Merged from lead L-1–L-75 and implementor I-1–I-39 against the proposal, design, canonical specs, and test plan. Every original ID is retained below; an ID repeated across rows means its compound behavior was split into separate checks. Source describes checklist provenance; `crosscheck` identifies obligations found in the definition that neither checklist explicitly covered.
+
+Evidence was recorded after implementation; every evidence file named below is in `/workspace/home/.agent-runner/projects/-artifacts--runtime-candidate-worktree/runs/audited-implement-change-2026-10-17T18-16-38-659687771Z/output/evidence/`. AT-001, AT-002 and AT-004 were run by the implementing agent following `SKILL.md` with a scripted user (no independent human or second agent); AT-003 used `chrome-devtools-axi`. Before execution these were planned checks. Unit and contract checks run under fast Vitest `npm test`; type fixtures also use TypeScript. INT/E2E/browser checks run in a separate npm script, including INT-001, INT-002, E2E-001, and E2E-002. `npm run verify` is the production browser gate. Required AT-001–AT-004 follow the public skill in disposable projects using `chrome-devtools-axi` (AXI), starting with a structure snapshot and then settled screenshots. Static skill checks do not substitute for required AT journeys. Record any unexecuted check as `not verified` when evidence is added. The repository has no hosted CI: do not add CI configuration to implement the test plan's “every pull request” execution wording (AGENTS.md takes precedence).
+
+The lead resolved the sample/transition conflict in [acceptance-assumptions.md](/workspace/home/.agent-runner/projects/-artifacts--runtime-candidate-worktree/runs/audited-implement-change-2026-10-17T18-16-38-659687771Z/output/acceptance-assumptions.md), section “Checklist merge: position/size morph and departure checks versus the accumulating sample”. The sample must keep its accumulating composition. L-4's sample position/size observation is replaced by equally strict browser fixture coverage; L-6/I-4 departures use that fixture. The fixture is test-owned, in a disposable/test-only app, and never shipped in the production registry or Landing. AT-003 sample evidence points to the fixture for departures when not applicable to the sample. This preserves the required kit behaviors without changing the canonical nine-step outline. No user decision is pending.
