@@ -0,0 +1,160 @@
+---
+name: presentation
+description: Creates or modifies a browser presentation (one evolving diagram scene moving through named steps) from a topic. Use when asked to make, build, extend or change a presentation, talk, or slide-style explainer in a web project. It interviews the user, scaffolds the scene kit when missing, generates the presentation, and verifies build, render and visual composition before reporting done.
+---
+
+# Presentation
+
+A presentation is **one scene that evolves through named steps**, not a deck of slides. Entities
+have stable identities; moving from step to step makes them move, resize, re-label, enter, or
+leave in place. Presentations render with a vendored React scene kit (`src/presentation-kit/`).
+The kit ships **no styling**: every presentation owns its colors, type, spacing and chrome look in
+plain CSS (unless the host project already uses a styling framework or the user asks for one).
+
+`SKILL_DIR` below is the directory containing this `SKILL.md`. Resolve every template and script
+path from it (`$SKILL_DIR/templates/...`, `$SKILL_DIR/scripts/...`), never from the working
+directory.
+
+## 1. Decide what the user wants
+
+- **Create** a presentation: go to step 2.
+- **Modify** an existing one: go to "Modify an existing presentation" below. Step 3 (detect and, if needed, scaffold) applies to modification too and runs before any edit.
+
+## 2. Gather the requirements, one question at a time
+
+Ask only for what is missing from the user's prompt, **one question per message**, in this order:
+
+1. The **topic** (and audience, if it changes the story).
+2. The **visual style** (mood, palette, typography, density).
+3. For each **step**: its title (one line), its caption (a paragraph for browse mode), and a
+   description of what the diagram shows, what morphs from the previous step, and what enters or
+   leaves.
+
+Rules:
+
+- Do not assume details the user can still provide. Do not invent a style or step content you
+  could have asked about.
+- The user controls the depth. If they choose to build with partial detail ("just build it"), do
+  so from what was captured; there is no completeness gate. They can iterate afterwards.
+- If the prompt already contains the topic, style and every step, go straight to building.
+- For a key or visually complex step you may draw an ASCII mockup and ask the user to confirm the
+  layout. Do not do this for every step.
+
+## 3. Resolve the target and scaffold what is missing
+
+Run, from the user's project directory:
+
+```bash
+node "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/scaffold.mjs" detect
+```
+
+It reports the resolved `appDir`, why, which of the three contract anchors exist, and which are
+`missing`:
+
+1. **build** — Vite + React + TypeScript app with a working `npm run build`.
+2. **kit** — `src/presentation-kit/` (the `Step`/`Scene` contract, stage, navigation, chrome).
+3. **index** — `src/presentations/index.ts`, the registry mapping each presentation to its route.
+
+Detection is by anchor, so cosmetic differences (file names, formatting, extra dependencies) do
+not trigger re-scaffolding. Target resolution:
+
+- Empty directory or standalone project → the repository root.
+- Monorepo (`workspaces`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, `lerna.json`, `turbo.json`, or a top-level
+  `packages/` or `apps/`) → a self-contained app in `presentations/`; never edit the monorepo root.
+- Already inside (or next to, in `presentations/`) a presentation app → use it.
+
+Then:
+
+- All anchors present → skip scaffolding.
+- Some missing → scaffold **only** the missing anchors; never disturb what exists.
+- If `needsConfirmation` is true (the project is not empty and something must be written), **state
+  the target directory and what will be written, and wait for the user to confirm** before running
+  `apply`. An empty directory needs no confirmation.
+
+```bash
+node "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/scaffold.mjs" apply            # add --target <dir> to follow a corrected target
+```
+
+`apply` also reports `notes` when something needs manual wiring (for example an existing `src/main.tsx` that does not render `<Router />`); do that wiring before continuing. `apply` copies the missing parts from `$SKILL_DIR/templates/bootstrap/`, never overwrites existing
+files (an incomplete existing kit folder is filled in file by file), merges `package.json` instead of replacing it (dependencies, `verify` and `inspect` scripts are added even when a build setup already exists), and runs `npm install` so the full
+dependency set is present (React, Vite, TypeScript and its types, Motion, Lucide, ESLint,
+Playwright). Do not assume any dependency is already installed. Playwright also needs a Chromium
+(`npx playwright install chromium` if none is available). The scaffold requires no Tailwind or other
+styling framework and defines no colors, fonts or component looks.
+
+## 4. Create the presentation
+
+Pick a lowercase hyphenated slug from the topic, then:
+
+```bash
+node "$SKILL_DIR/scripts/scaffold.mjs" create <slug> "<Title>" --app <appDir>
+```
+
+This copies `$SKILL_DIR/templates/presentation/` to `src/presentations/<slug>/` and adds the
+registry line to `src/presentations/index.ts`. Existing presentations are untouched. Then replace
+the template's content with the user's story. Read `references/authoring.md` for the kit API and
+the conventions below:
+
+- `entities.ts` — the presentation's `layoutId` namespace (stable ids).
+- `steps.ts` — one `Step` per beat: `id`, `era`, `title` (one line), `caption` (paragraph), `Scene`,
+  and a typed `payload`. Give consecutive steps of one diagram the same `groupKey` and `Scene` so
+  the scene persists and entities morph in place instead of remounting.
+- `Scene.tsx` — composes kit primitives (`Box`, `Label`, `Arrow`, `Frame`, `Emphasis`,
+  `SymbolChip`, `Appear`, `SceneLayer`) on the fixed 880 × 380 canvas. Entities that persist keep
+  their id and change position, size, label or emphasis; wrap newcomers in `Appear` so they enter
+  after the others settle; wrap leavers' presence in `Appear when={…}` so they animate out.
+- `talk.css` — **all** styling, in this presentation's own plain CSS, targeting the kit's
+  `data-presentation-*` hooks. Style the active progress item and active table-of-contents entry
+  (`[data-presentation-active]`) so the current step is clearly distinct, and style
+  `[data-presentation-attribution]` so the "made by and-scene" link is legible. Never add styles,
+  colors or fonts to `src/presentation-kit/`.
+
+## 5. Verify before reporting done
+
+All of these must pass. If any fails, fix the cause and re-run; never report success on a failure.
+
+1. `npm run lint` and `npm run build` — no type errors.
+2. `npm run verify` — builds the app and renders every step of every registered presentation in
+   Chromium on `127.0.0.1`, failing on any console or page error.
+3. Visual composition — run the project-local screenshot helper (prefer it over ad hoc scripts;
+   if it is missing, write any temporary Playwright script under the project root so it resolves
+   local dependencies):
+
+   ```bash
+   npm run inspect -- <slug>            # desktop 1440 × 900 → inspection-output/<slug>/step-NN.png
+   npm run inspect -- <slug> --narrow   # 390 × 844 → inspection-output/<slug>-narrow/
+   ```
+
+   The helper waits for animations to settle before each capture. Open the screenshots (or inspect
+   the page with `chrome-devtools-axi`: `snapshot`, then `screenshot`) for the **first step, the last
+   step, and every dense or key step**; also check a narrow viewport when the presentation is
+   responsive-sensitive. Confirm important content fits the canvas, intentional overlaps stay
+   readable, and nothing collides with the caption, progress dots, table of contents, controls or
+   attribution.
+4. Review every `WARN step N …` line the helper prints. They are advisory, but each must be
+   resolved: fix accidental collisions; make active chrome visibly distinct; style the
+   attribution through its hook. Only mark a subtree with `data-presentation-allow-overlap` when
+   the overlap is intentional and readable, and mark just that subtree. Re-run the helper after
+   fixing, and report any warnings that remain, accurately.
+
+The screenshot directory `inspection-output/` is gitignored; do not commit screenshots or `dist/`.
+
+## Modify an existing presentation
+
+0. Run step 3 first (`scaffold.mjs detect`): modification needs the kit, the registry and the build setup too. If an anchor is missing, scaffold it (with the confirmation rule) before editing anything.
+1. Identify the target. If the user did not name one, or the name is ambiguous, list the
+   presentations from `src/presentations/index.ts` (slug and title) and ask which one **before
+   changing anything**.
+2. Ask only about the requested changes (steps, entities or style). Do not re-run the create
+   interview.
+3. Edit only that presentation's folder (and the registry only if its title or slug must change).
+   Keep entity ids stable so existing morphs still work.
+4. Run the same verification as step 5.
+
+## Quality bar
+
+A generated presentation builds with no type errors, renders its first step with no runtime or
+console errors, shows a caption per step, supports next/previous navigation, passes the visual
+composition check, and follows the evolving-scene model: one scene, stable entity identities,
+numbered by position, with a present mode (title only) and a browse mode (caption, table of
+contents, controls, progress).
diff --git a/skills/presentation/references/authoring.md b/skills/presentation/references/authoring.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..98c43ed9857861b625b2872474d5a7a82c8f137f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/skills/presentation/references/authoring.md
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+# Scene kit authoring reference
+
+Import everything from `../../presentation-kit/index.ts` inside `src/presentations/<slug>/`.
+
+## Step contract
+
+```ts
+interface Step<TPayload> {
+  id: string          // stable identity
+  era: string         // section label; consecutive equal eras form one table-of-contents entry
+  title: string       // one line, shown in present and browse mode
+  caption: string     // paragraph, shown in browse mode
+  Scene: ComponentType<SceneProps<TPayload>>
+  groupKey?: string   // same groupKey + same Scene => one mounted scene, only `payload` changes
+  payload: TPayload   // typed state for this beat (optional when TPayload is undefined)
+}
+```
+
+Step numbers come from position; never number steps by hand. `<Presentation steps={STEPS}
+title="…" initialMode="browse" className="…" />` accepts a typed `Step<P>[]` without casts.
+
+## Primitives (all style-neutral)
+
+| Primitive | Use |
+| --- | --- |
+| `Box` | positioned entity; `id` is its `layoutId`; optional `icon={LucideIcon}`; `kind` names it in `data-presentation-node` |
+| `Label` | free text entity |
+| `SymbolChip` | small icon/text entity |
+| `Frame` | outline drawn around other entities (look comes from your CSS) |
+| `Arrow` | line or curve (`from`, `to`, optional `curve`, `bidirectional`, `when`); stroke follows `currentColor` |
+| `Emphasis` | highlight marker that fades in/out (`active`) |
+| `Appear` | `when` controls presence: newcomers enter after persisting entities settle, leavers animate out |
+| `SceneLayer` | absolutely positioned layer filling the canvas |
+
+All accept `className`/`style`. Position with `style={{ left, top, width, height }}` in canvas units
+(880 × 380); the stage scales the canvas uniformly to fit. For coordinate-heavy diagrams you may use
+raw `motion` elements with stable `layoutId`s.
+
+## Motion rules
+
+- Persisting entity: same `id` in both steps; change `left/top/width/height`, text, or a data
+  attribute and it morphs in place. Do not wrap a persisting entity in `Appear` that toggles.
+- Newcomer: `Appear when={beat >= n}` (enters after layout morphs finish).
+- Leaver: `Appear when={beat < n}` (animates out).
+- Intentional overlaps and stacks are fine; mark readable ones with `data-presentation-allow-overlap`.
+
+## Hooks for your CSS
+
+`[data-presentation-root]` (with `data-presentation-mode`, `-step-count`, `-step-index`),
+`-header`, `-brand`, `-deck-title`, `-toc`, `-toc-item`, `-narration`, `-marker`, `-title`,
+`-caption`, `-footer`, `-prev`, `-next`, `-progress`, `-progress-item`, `-attribution`,
+`-stage`, `-canvas`, `-node`, `-id`. Active progress/ToC entries carry `data-presentation-active`
+and `aria-current`.
diff --git a/skills/presentation/scripts/scaffold.mjs b/skills/presentation/scripts/scaffold.mjs
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..aa8d5d624a486aaa8a28a6892255b4352a5cc165
--- /dev/null
+++ b/skills/presentation/scripts/scaffold.mjs
@@ -0,0 +1,271 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env node
+// Detects and scaffolds the infrastructure a generated presentation depends on.
+//   node scaffold.mjs detect [dir]                      print the resolved target and missing anchors as JSON
+//   node scaffold.mjs apply [dir] [--target <dir>] [--no-install] [--starter]
+//   node scaffold.mjs create <slug> "<Title>" [--app <dir>]   add a new presentation folder and registry line
+// Templates are resolved relative to this file (the skill directory), never the working directory.
+import { spawnSync } from 'node:child_process'
+import { cp, mkdir, readdir, readFile, stat, writeFile } from 'node:fs/promises'
+import path from 'node:path'
+import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'
+
+const skillDir = path.resolve(path.dirname(fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)), '..')
+export const BOOTSTRAP_DIR = path.join(skillDir, 'templates', 'bootstrap')
+export const PRESENTATION_TEMPLATE_DIR = path.join(skillDir, 'templates', 'presentation')
+
+/** `--workspaces=false` keeps a nested app's install (lockfile, node_modules) out of a monorepo root. */
+export const INSTALL_ARGS = ['install', '--workspaces=false']
+
+const IGNORED = new Set(['.git', '.DS_Store'])
+const MONOREPO_FILES = ['pnpm-workspace.yaml', 'lerna.json', 'turbo.json']
+const MONOREPO_DIRS = ['packages', 'apps']
+
+const exists = (p) => stat(p).then(() => true, () => false)
+const readJson = (p) => readFile(p, 'utf8').then(JSON.parse, () => null)
+
+async function visibleEntries(dir) {
+  return (await readdir(dir).catch(() => [])).filter((name) => !IGNORED.has(name))
+}
+
+export async function isMonorepo(dir) {
+  const pkg = await readJson(path.join(dir, 'package.json'))
+  if (pkg?.workspaces) return true
+  for (const file of MONOREPO_FILES) if (await exists(path.join(dir, file))) return true
+  for (const sub of MONOREPO_DIRS) if (await exists(path.join(dir, sub))) return true
+  return false
+}
+
+/** Contract-level anchor detection: keyed on what exists, not on a byte-identical scaffold. */
+export async function detectAnchors(dir) {
+  const pkg = await readJson(path.join(dir, 'package.json'))
+  const deps = { ...pkg?.dependencies, ...pkg?.devDependencies }
+  const viteConfig = (await visibleEntries(dir)).some((name) => /^vite\.config\.[cm]?[jt]s$/.test(name))
+  const build = Boolean(pkg?.scripts?.build && deps.vite && deps.react && deps.typescript && viteConfig)
+
+  let kit = false
+  for (const name of ['index.ts', 'index.tsx']) {
+    const source = await readFile(path.join(dir, 'src', 'presentation-kit', name), 'utf8').catch(() => '')
+    if (/\bPresentation\b/.test(source)) kit = true
+  }
+  const index = (await visibleEntries(path.join(dir, 'src', 'presentations'))).some((name) => /^index\.[jt]sx?$/.test(name))
+  return { build, kit, index }
+}
+
+const missingOf = (anchors) => Object.keys(anchors).filter((name) => !anchors[name])
+
+/** Resolves where the presentation app lives and which anchors it lacks. */
+export async function detect(cwd) {
+  const entries = await visibleEntries(cwd)
+  const empty = entries.length === 0
+  const monorepo = await isMonorepo(cwd)
+  const nested = path.join(cwd, 'presentations')
+
+  const here = await detectAnchors(cwd)
+  const inNested = await detectAnchors(nested)
+  let appDir = cwd
+  let reason = 'standalone or empty project: scaffold at the repository root'
+  if (here.kit || here.index) {
+    reason = 'the current directory already is a presentation app'
+  } else if (inNested.kit || inNested.index) {
+    appDir = nested
+    reason = 'an existing presentation app lives in presentations/'
+  } else if (monorepo && !empty) {
+    appDir = nested
+    reason = 'monorepo detected: scaffold a self-contained app in presentations/'
+  }
+  const anchors = appDir === cwd ? here : inNested
+  const missing = missingOf(anchors)
+  return {
+    cwd,
+    appDir,
+    reason,
+    empty,
+    monorepo,
+    anchors,
+    missing,
+    // Writing scaffold files into a non-empty project needs the user's confirmation of the target first.
+    needsConfirmation: !empty && missing.length > 0,
+  }
+}
+
+/** Copies a file or directory tree, filling in only what is absent; existing files are never touched. */
+async function copyIfAbsent(source, target, written, skipped) {
+  if ((await stat(source)).isDirectory()) {
+    for (const name of await readdir(source)) await copyIfAbsent(path.join(source, name), path.join(target, name), written, skipped)
+    return
+  }
+  if (await exists(target)) {
+    skipped.push(target)
+    return
+  }
+  await mkdir(path.dirname(target), { recursive: true })
+  await cp(source, target)
+  written.push(target)
+}
+
+async function mergePackageJson(appDir, written) {
+  const target = path.join(appDir, 'package.json')
+  const template = await readJson(path.join(BOOTSTRAP_DIR, 'package.json'))
+  const current = await readJson(target)
+  if (!current) {
+    await writeFile(target, `${JSON.stringify(template, null, 2)}\n`)
+    written.push(target)
+    return
+  }
+  const alreadyHas = (name) => name in { ...current.dependencies, ...current.devDependencies }
+  const merged = { ...current, type: current.type ?? template.type }
+  merged.scripts = { ...template.scripts, ...current.scripts }
+  for (const section of ['dependencies', 'devDependencies']) {
+    const add = Object.fromEntries(Object.entries(template[section] ?? {}).filter(([name]) => !alreadyHas(name)))
+    merged[section] = { ...current[section], ...add }
+  }
+  await writeFile(target, `${JSON.stringify(merged, null, 2)}\n`)
+  written.push(target)
+}
+
+const BUILD_FILES = [
+  'index.html',
+  'vite.config.ts',
+  'tsconfig.json',
+  'tsconfig.app.json',
+  'tsconfig.node.json',
+  'eslint.config.js',
+  'src/main.tsx',
+  'src/index.css',
+]
+const INDEX_FILES = ['src/Router.tsx', 'src/router.ts', 'src/Landing.tsx']
+/** The registry module, whatever its extension. */
+async function registryFile(appDir) {
+  for (const name of ['index.ts', 'index.tsx', 'index.js', 'index.jsx']) {
+    const file = path.join(appDir, 'src', 'presentations', name)
+    if (await exists(file)) return file
+  }
+  return null
+}
+
+const REGISTRY = `import type { ComponentType } from 'react'
+
+export interface PresentationEntry {
+  slug: string
+  title: string
+  load: () => Promise<{ default: ComponentType }>
+}
+
+/** Explicit registry: adding a presentation is a new folder plus one line here. */
+export const presentations: PresentationEntry[] = []
+`
+
+/** Copies the templates for the missing anchors without overwriting anything that exists. */
+export async function apply(appDir, missing, { starter = false, install = true } = {}) {
+  const written = []
+  const skipped = []
+  await mkdir(appDir, { recursive: true })
+  const from = (rel) => path.join(BOOTSTRAP_DIR, rel)
+  const to = (rel) => path.join(appDir, rel)
+
+  if (missing.length) {
+    // dependencies, scripts and verification tooling every presentation needs, whatever was already there
+    const hadPackage = await exists(to('package.json'))
+    await mergePackageJson(appDir, written)
+    if (!hadPackage) await copyIfAbsent(from('package-lock.json'), to('package-lock.json'), written, skipped)
+    for (const rel of ['scripts', 'verify.config.json']) await copyIfAbsent(from(rel), to(rel), written, skipped)
+    const ignore = to('.gitignore')
+    if (await exists(ignore)) {
+      const lines = (await readFile(ignore, 'utf8')).split('\n')
+      const extra = (await readFile(from('.gitignore'), 'utf8')).split('\n').filter((l) => l && !lines.includes(l))
+      if (extra.length) await writeFile(ignore, `${lines.join('\n').replace(/\n*$/, '\n')}${extra.join('\n')}\n`)
+    } else {
+      await copyIfAbsent(from('.gitignore'), ignore, written, skipped)
+    }
+  }
+  if (missing.includes('build')) {
+    for (const rel of BUILD_FILES) await copyIfAbsent(from(rel), to(rel), written, skipped)
+  }
+  if (missing.includes('kit')) {
+    await copyIfAbsent(from('src/presentation-kit'), to('src/presentation-kit'), written, skipped)
+  }
+  if (missing.includes('index')) {
+    for (const rel of INDEX_FILES) await copyIfAbsent(from(rel), to(rel), written, skipped)
+    if (starter) {
+      await copyIfAbsent(from('src/presentations'), to('src/presentations'), written, skipped)
+    } else if (!(await registryFile(appDir))) {
+      await mkdir(to('src/presentations'), { recursive: true })
+      await writeFile(to('src/presentations/index.ts'), REGISTRY)
+      written.push(to('src/presentations/index.ts'))
+    }
+  }
+  const notes = []
+  const entry = await readFile(to('src/main.tsx'), 'utf8').catch(() => null)
+  if (missing.includes('index') && entry !== null && !/\bRouter\b/.test(entry)) {
+    notes.push('src/main.tsx exists but does not render <Router />: wire it (see templates/bootstrap/src/main.tsx) so presentation routes work')
+  }
+
+  let installed = false
+  if (install && missing.length) {
+    const result = spawnSync('npm', INSTALL_ARGS, { cwd: appDir, stdio: 'inherit' })
+    installed = result.status === 0
+    if (!installed) throw new Error('npm install failed in ' + appDir)
+  }
+  return { appDir, written, skipped, installed, notes }
+}
+
+/** Fills the placeholders of the new-presentation template. */
+export function fillTemplate(text, slug, title) {
+  // `__TITLE_JSON__` is a JS string literal (safe inside TSX attributes); `__TITLE__` is the raw text
+  return text.replaceAll('__SLUG__', slug).replaceAll('__TITLE_JSON__', JSON.stringify(title)).replaceAll('__TITLE__', title)
+}
+
+export const SLUG_PATTERN = /^[a-z0-9]+(?:-[a-z0-9]+)*$/
+
+/** Adds a registry entry to an `index.ts` source, keeping the explicit-array format. */
+export function addRegistryEntry(source, slug, title) {
+  const open = /\bpresentations\b[^=\n;]*=\s*\[/.exec(source)
+  const close = source.lastIndexOf(']')
+  if (!open || close < open.index + open[0].length) throw new Error('could not find the presentations array in the registry')
+  const quoted = `'${title.replaceAll('\\', '\\\\').replaceAll("'", "\\'")}'`
+  const entry = `  {\n    slug: '${slug}',\n    title: ${quoted},\n    load: () => import('./${slug}/Talk.tsx'),\n  },\n`
+  let body = source.slice(open.index + open[0].length, close).replace(/\s*$/, '')
+  if (body && !body.endsWith(',')) body += ','
+  return `${source.slice(0, open.index + open[0].length)}${body}\n${entry}${source.slice(close)}`
+}
+
+/** Creates `src/presentations/<slug>/` from the presentation template and registers it. */
+export async function createPresentation(appDir, slug, title) {
+  if (!SLUG_PATTERN.test(slug)) throw new Error(`invalid slug "${slug}" (use lowercase words joined by hyphens)`)
+  const folder = path.join(appDir, 'src', 'presentations', slug)
+  const registryPath = await registryFile(appDir)
+  if (!registryPath) throw new Error('no presentation registry (src/presentations/index.*) found')
+  if (await exists(folder)) throw new Error(`presentation "${slug}" already exists`)
+  const registry = await readFile(registryPath, 'utf8')
+  const updated = addRegistryEntry(registry, slug, title)
+  await mkdir(folder, { recursive: true })
+  for (const name of await readdir(PRESENTATION_TEMPLATE_DIR)) {
+    const text = await readFile(path.join(PRESENTATION_TEMPLATE_DIR, name), 'utf8')
+    await writeFile(path.join(folder, name), fillTemplate(text, slug, title))
+  }
+  await writeFile(registryPath, updated)
+  return { folder, registryFile: registryPath }
+}
+
+if (process.argv[1] === fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)) {
+  const [command, ...rest] = process.argv.slice(2)
+  const flag = (name) => rest.includes(name)
+  const value = (name) => (rest.includes(name) ? rest[rest.indexOf(name) + 1] : undefined)
+  const positional = rest.filter((arg, i) => !arg.startsWith('--') && rest[i - 1] !== '--target')[0]
+  const cwd = path.resolve(positional ?? process.cwd())
+  const detected = command === 'create' ? null : await detect(cwd)
+  if (command === 'create') {
+    const [slug, title] = rest.filter((arg, i) => !arg.startsWith('--') && rest[i - 1] !== '--app')
+    const appDir = path.resolve(value('--app') ?? (await detect(process.cwd())).appDir)
+    console.log(JSON.stringify(await createPresentation(appDir, slug, title ?? slug), null, 2))
+  } else if (command === 'detect') {
+    console.log(JSON.stringify(detected, null, 2))
+  } else if (command === 'apply') {
+    const appDir = path.resolve(value('--target') ?? detected.appDir)
+    const anchors = appDir === detected.appDir ? detected.missing : missingOf(await detectAnchors(appDir))
+    console.log(JSON.stringify(await apply(appDir, anchors, { starter: flag('--starter'), install: !flag('--no-install') }), null, 2))
+  } else {
+    console.error('usage: scaffold.mjs detect|apply|create [dir] [--target <dir>] [--no-install] [--starter]')
+    process.exit(2)
+  }
+}
